---
source: crates/leptoskit_cli/tests/snapshots.rs
expression: "normalize(&stdout(&output), &scratch.path)"
---
Prepare candidates, recheck inputs, then activate each host

Usage: leptoskit infra release apply [OPTIONS] --bundle <BUNDLE> --sha256 <SHA256> --trust <TRUST> --trust-sha256 <TRUST_SHA256> --version <VERSION> --unit <UNIT> --plan <PLAN>

Options:
      --app-target <NAME>
          Select a named target from the root leptoskit.toml
      --bundle <BUNDLE>
          Directory containing captured graph artifacts and manifest.json
      --sha256 <SHA256>
          Independently obtained graph manifest digest
      --trust <TRUST>
          Independently maintained host/runtime trust document
      --trust-sha256 <TRUST_SHA256>
          Independently obtained SHA-256 of the host/runtime trust document
      --caddy <CADDY>
          Supplied Linux Caddy executable; required only for selected public hosts
      --caddy-sha256 <CADDY_SHA256>
          Independently obtained SHA-256 of the Linux Caddy executable
      --version <VERSION>
          Release identifier; rollback selects a previously installed version
      --unit <UNIT>
          Selected graph unit, such as frontends.docs; repeat for multiple units
      --plan <PLAN>
          Saved plan file. Apply/status/rollback compare it to current inputs
      --recover-plan-sha256 <RECOVER_PLAN_SHA256>
          Recover an existing operation using the independently obtained digest of its original saved plan. Retains historical operation/host identities
      --policy <POLICY>
          Graph approvals are not implemented; strict fails before mutation [default: operator] [possible values: operator, strict]
  -h, --help
          Print help
